## Framework-Agnostic Error Design

### Current Problem
- NegotiateRejection implements axum::response::IntoResponse
- Couples core library to axum

### Proposed Solution

#### 1. Core Error Type (framework-agnostic)
```rust
#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
pub enum NegotiateError {
    BodyRead(String),
    Deserialize(String),
    UnsupportedMediaType(String),
}

impl std::error::Error for NegotiateError {}

impl NegotiateError {
    pub fn status_code(&self) -> http::StatusCode {
        match self {
            Self::BodyRead(_) => StatusCode::BAD_REQUEST,
            Self::Deserialize(_) => StatusCode::BAD_REQUEST,
            Self::UnsupportedMediaType(_) => StatusCode::UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE,
        }
    }
}
```

#### 2. Framework Adapters (feature-gated)
```rust
#[cfg(feature = "axum")]
impl IntoResponse for NegotiateError {
    fn into_response(self) -> Response {
        (self.status_code(), self.to_string()).into_response()
    }
}
```

### Key Principles
1. Core error implements std::error::Error only
2. Exposes status_code() method for adapters
3. IntoResponse impl moves to axum feature flag
4. Pattern from tonic::Status, tower-http

### Migration Path
1. Introduce NegotiateError in parallel
2. Deprecate NegotiateRejection
3. Feature-gate IntoResponse impl
